# This repository is LF, on every machine, whatever a developer's global
# core.autocrlf happens to say. We work on macOS, Linux and Windows/WSL2, and
# the line endings cannot be left to whichever of those a checkout landed on.
#
# A CRLF checkout is not a cosmetic difference here: gofmt reports every Go file
# as unformatted, so `make ci` fails on fmt-check before it runs a single test,
# and the diff of a one-line change is the whole file. eol=lf overrides
# core.autocrlf, which is what makes this a property of the repository rather
# than of the machine that cloned it.
#
# text=auto lets git detect binary content and leave it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets git must never treat as text, whatever its detection concludes.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
